winecoreaudio.drv: Wine 11.21's SpatialMixer downmix, backported to winecx (e0aa380).

The five commits by Zhiyi Zhang (CodeWeavers) from Wine 11.21, in order, applied unchanged to
dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c (they apply with line offsets only):
  199ae1d33c5adee0e126c71108998ea315c19ed4 winecoreaudio.drv: Move some helpers.
  d20f6c71e746b76cd0cc19307c4c56e222526826 winecoreaudio.drv: Add a get_format_channel_mask() helper.
  3e29c3639e852fd9cfad8dc4d0a85015d7ab3f80 winecoreaudio.drv: Add a ca_get_layout_channel_mask() helper.
  8cf640803ba9ab35fb6743fec5553e47faa34d56 winecoreaudio.drv: Add a get_device_channel_mask() helper.
  0c61795bfd04e290fb3966cb0f62f869d0d84443 winecoreaudio.drv: Add a SpatialMixer audio unit to mix
                                           input audio when necessary.
HALOutput maps channels but doesn't mix them down: a 5.1/7.1 stream whose channel mask differs
from the device's lost channels or put them in the wrong speakers (GTA V Enhanced's dialogue,
Lego Star Wars on stereo; possibly the echo on an AV receiver set to "7.1 wide"). In shared mode
with more than two channels and a mask other than the device's, a SpatialMixer now mixes them.
CrossOver's capture-authorization code in the same file stays as it is.

